//www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/","lastmod":"2026-08-21T20:42:16+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-08-21 21:20:31"},{"competitor_name":"AADOM","domain":"www.dentalmanagers.com","url":"https://www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/planning-your-way-to-victory/","lastmod":"2024-09-12T20:29:57+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-12 09:22:07"},{"competitor_name":"AADOM","domain":"www.dentalmanagers.com","url":"https://www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/balancing-innovation-and-tradition/","lastmod":"2024-09-12T19:58:58+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-11 09:22:21"},{"competitor_name":"AADOM","domain":"www.dentalmanagers.com","url":"https://www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/reviving-team-engagement-rotating-leadership-and-structured-agendas/","lastmod":"2024-09-12T17:55:58+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-11 09:22:21"},{"competitor_name":"AADOM","domain":"www.dentalmanagers.com","url":"https://www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/8-ways-to-keep-your-a-r-down-and-your-collection-percentages-up/","lastmod":"2024-09-12T17:24:48+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-04 09:09:24"},{"competitor_name":"AADOM","domain":"www.dentalmanagers.com","url":"https://www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/say-goodbye-to-the-front-vs-back-battle/","lastmod":"2024-09-12T16:33:50+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-04 09:09:24"},{"competitor_name":"AADOM","domain":"www.dentalmanagers.com","url":"https://www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/creating-magic-in-pediatric-dentistry/","lastmod":"2024-09-12T15:00:11+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-08-28 09:19:24"},{"competitor_name":"AADOM","domain":"www.dentalmanagers.com","url":"https://www.dentalmanagers.com/blog/5-ways-to-bridge-the-generational-divide/","lastmod":"2024-09-12T14:17:11+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-08-28 09:19:24"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/operational-efficiency-in-dental-practice-with-ai/","lastmod":"2026-09-10T15:20:34+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-11 09:22:26"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/dental-reviews-need-a-growth-system/","lastmod":"2026-09-09T18:02:51+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-10 09:23:03"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/dental-office-systems-for-perio-care/","lastmod":"2026-09-07T19:43:30+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-08 09:08:57"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/dental-case-acceptance-with-confidence/","lastmod":"2026-09-03T15:12:37+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-04 09:09:32"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/dental-technology-needs-better-systems/","lastmod":"2026-08-31T14:57:58+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-09-01 09:20:48"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/get-your-life-back-without-losing-growth/","lastmod":"2026-08-27T16:20:38+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-08-28 09:19:30"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/dental-kpis-tell-more-than-one-story/","lastmod":"2026-08-26T15:22:45+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-08-26 22:40:38"},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","domain":"www.thedentalateam.com","url":"https://www.thedentalateam.com/blogs/dental-practice-growth-through-community/","lastmod":"2026-08-24T17:43:24+00:00","first_seen_at":"2026-08-25 09:19:44"}],"totals":[{"competitor_name":"AADOM","total_pages_tracked":810},{"competitor_name":"Dental A Team","total_pages_tracked":808}],"checked_at":"2026-09-12 09:22:07"},"serp_competitors":{"available":false,"competitors":[],"checked_at":null},"ad_spy":{"available":false,"entries":[],"by_competitor":[],"last_updated":null},"team_meetings":{"available":true,"meetings":[{"id":4,"meeting_date":"2026-09-11","title":"DOMA Team Meeting Recap","summary":"Mariannel's status still TBD - Kyle meets GetVWire Monday, Michelle covering in the meantime. Two new sponsors: Cherry (patient financing) and Vine Dental (insurance verification); Mark3 dropped. Events strategy shifting toward tagging onto sponsor events instead of DOMA running its own. Ask DOMA (Replit AI tool) is framework-only, going to the Advisory Board for feedback next. Avg position up to 13.1 (+1.6). ActiveCampaign clearly outperforming GoHighLevel (1,019 vs 83 opens on the same Sep 2 send) - GHL likely landing in spam.","raw_notes":"👋 DOMA Team Meeting Recap (Sep 11)\nKyle, Lucas & Juli\n\nQuick but productive — here's everything covered today 👇\n\n👥 TEAM UPDATE — MARIANNEL SITUATION\nStill TBD on Mariannel's status. Kyle has a meeting with GetVWire on Monday to find out what's happening. Michelle has been brought in as a possible replacement — she's with us for now.\n\nGoing forward until Monday:\n\nDon't assign anything major to Michelle today\nAfter Monday's call Kyle will know if Mariannel is coming back or if Michelle is the permanent replacement\nWhen passing tasks to Michelle, add more context than usual — she may not be fully up to speed yet\nJuli — if it turns out Mariannel is gone, you can be trained on the custom GPT ebook process as a backup\n\nEbook topic cadence going forward:\n\nJuli to supply ebook topics every Monday for the week (3 per week)\nTopics pulled from the dashboard content suggestions (mix of Google Search Console data + top performing ebooks)\nData speaks for itself — let the algorithm guide the topics, not guesswork\n\n🤝 NEW SPONSORS — WELCOME CHERRY & VINE DENTAL\n\nTwo new sponsors are in! Here's the quick rundown:\n\nCherry — dental patient financing (similar to CareCredit). Jason is the marketing contact (based in Israel). Kyle has a call with them Monday at 10am to discuss content strategy — they're interested in going beyond a standard sponsorship (possible events involvement, content creation).\n\nVine Dental — dental insurance verification platform. Andy is the contact. He hasn't confirmed a meeting yet. Also does their own annual event (Accelerate Revenue Workshop — Oct 22–24) which could be an opportunity to tag on.\n\nMark3 — removed ❌\nThey wanted guarantees we can't provide and were consistently asking for more than their contract included. After 6 months Kyle ended the relationship. Dr. Glen Vo's group is doing the same.\n\nLucas — website updates needed:\n\nAdd Cherry and Vine Dental logos to the homepage sponsor carousel\nAdd both to the Offers page — describe what they do, link to their main websites for now\nRemove Mark3 from everywhere on the site\nFix the Roya logo — currently unreadable\nJuli to send Lucas both website links tonight via WhatsApp\n\n🎟️ EVENTS STRATEGY UPDATE\n\nNo rush on events right now. Kyle is watching what others in the space are doing before committing. Key observations:\n\nSeveral groups are now trying big pop-up events and luxury experiences — Kyle has been through this and knows how draining and expensive it is\nArchie still hasn't sent materials for the October event despite promising to. Kyle may push it back — there's not enough time to promote a 5-week-out event with nothing in hand\nNew event model being shaped: Rather than DOMA running its own events, the plan is to tag onto sponsor events — bring our audience, get a table or speaking slot, let them handle logistics\nVine Dental's event (Oct 22–24) could be a first test of this model\nCherry call Monday will also explore potential event partnership\n\nWebsite rename coming eventually:\n\"DOMA Pop-Up Events\" and \"DOMA Academy Live\" will eventually just become \"DOMA Events\" — cleaner and more flexible. No rush, Lucas will update when the time is right.\n\n🤖 ASK DOMA — PRODUCT CONCEPT UPDATE\n\nKyle showed the team the \"Ask DOMA\" support tool built in Replit — a custom AI tool where dental office managers can ask practice management questions and get answers formatted in Kyle's teaching style.\n\nCurrent state: framework only — no data populated behind it yet. It asks the right questions (role, context, etc.) and routes to the right answer, but the library needs to be built out.\n\nNext step: Present it to the Advisory Board — give them the link, ask them to play with it and share feedback. Good way to get real user input before investing more build time.\n\nJuli's insight: The real value vs. generic ChatGPT is that this tool already expects the dental context and formats answers the way Kyle teaches. The prompt is pre-built. That's the differentiator.\n\nLucas — action: Get familiar with Replit from a technical standpoint when time allows.\n\n📊 METRICS SNAPSHOT\n\nSEO:\n\nAverage position: 13.1 (up 1.6) — rankings improving ✅\nGoogle takes 1–2 weeks to reflect indexing changes — keep in mind when evaluating results\nTwo new blog articles published — Lucas waiting one more week to analyze performance before adjusting\n\nEmail Campaigns:\n\nActiveCampaign is outperforming GoHighLevel — Sep 2 AC send: 1,019 unique opens vs. GoHighLevel: 83 opens on the same day\nGoHighLevel emails appear to be landing in spam for many recipients\nRevenue Well is happy — they're asking about building a formal marketing package. Kyle to put something together\n\nContent Calendar:\n\nCurrently filled through yesterday — Juli to update through two weeks ahead this week\nJuli to follow up with Lucas on which content calendar items are getting posted vs. sitting — some aren't making it live\n\nDashboard:\n\nLucas added a new email performance tab — updating metrics by end of day today\nConsent bar added to the website (good for Google compliance)\n\nVideos:\n\nLucas sent Kyle 3 video versions for review — waiting on feedback for which style to move forward with\nJuli's first video almost done — Lucas finalizing by end of day\nBest posting day/time confirmed: Tuesday @ 9am ET\n\n🏘️ FACEBOOK GROUP — MODERATION REMINDER\n\nModeration expectations for Juli:\n\nIf you see a comment that shouldn't be there and you have time — remove it\nIf you don't have time — screenshot it or drop the post link in WhatsApp and flag it. Someone else will get to it\nPages (not personal profiles) commenting = automatic removal\nCompetitor group promotions = remove the comment + remove the person\nYou don't have to catch everything but flag what you notice\n\nAdVent Technologies — they commented on something as a page. Flag for removal.\n\n✅ KYLE — ACTION ITEMS\n\nMonday meeting with GetVWire — determine Mariannel vs. Michelle going forward\nMonday 10am — Cherry call (content strategy + possible events)\nFollow up with Vine Dental's Andy about scheduling a meeting\nSend Juli the Advisory Board mastermind recap (still owed from last week)\nReview the 3 video versions Lucas sent and pick a direction\nPut together a marketing package concept for Revenue Well\nLook into Vine Dental's October event as a potential tag-on opportunity\n\n✅ JULI — ACTION ITEMS\n\nSend Cherry and Vine Dental website links to Lucas tonight via WhatsApp\nSend Welcome email to Vine Dental's Andy (sponsor intro + deliverables)\nWait until Monday before giving Michelle ebook topics — confirm who's staying after Kyle's call\nStarting Monday: supply ebook topics every week (3 per week, data-driven from dashboard)\nUpdate content calendar through two weeks ahead — this week\nFollow up with Lucas on which calendar items are actually getting posted\nFollow up with Anna about her article — still outstanding\nStill owe Jocelyn a return call — connect this week\nIf you see rogue comments or page posts in the Facebook group — screenshot and flag in WhatsApp\nContinue filming short videos — send raw footage to Lucas\n\n✅ LUCAS — ACTION ITEMS\n\nAdd Cherry + Vine Dental to homepage sponsor carousel and Offers page (Juli sending links tonight)\nCreate Welcome Image for New sponsor to be shared on FB Page and Announcement in our group\nRemove Mark3 from everywhere on the website\nFix Roya logo (currently unreadable)\nUpdate email performance tab in dashboard — by end of today\nFinalize Juli's video — by end of today\nContinue monitoring AC vs. GoHighLevel performance — AC is winning, keep sending newsletters through AC\nGet familiar with Replit when bandwidth allows\nCheck which content calendar items are not going live and why — sync with Juli\n\n🗓️ NEXT MEETINGS\n\nMonday Sep 15 — Kyle + GetVWire (Mariannel/Michelle decision)\nMonday Sep 15 @ 10am — Kyle + Cherry (marketing strategy call)\nNext team meeting TBD — Kyle traveling again next week will confirm in WhatsApp\n\nAppreciate the team holding things down while I've been in transition mode — great work everyone! 💪🦷\n","action_items":[{"id":44,"owner":"Juli","description":"Send Cherry and Vine Dental website links to Lucas via WhatsApp","status":"open","context":"Same night as the meeting.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Sponsors"},{"id":45,"owner":"Juli","description":"Send welcome email to Vine Dental's Andy","status":"open","context":"Sponsor intro + deliverables.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Sponsors"},{"id":46,"owner":"Juli","description":"Wait until Monday before giving Michelle ebook topics","status":"open","context":"Confirm who's staying (Mariannel vs. Michelle) after Kyle's GetVWire call first.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":47,"owner":"Juli","description":"Supply ebook topics every Monday going forward (3 per week)","status":"open","context":"Pulled from dashboard content suggestions (GSC data + top-performing ebooks) - data-driven, not guesswork.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":48,"owner":"Juli","description":"Update content calendar through two weeks ahead","status":"open","context":"Currently only filled through yesterday.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content Calendar"},{"id":49,"owner":"Juli","description":"Follow up with Lucas on which calendar items are actually getting posted vs. sitting","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Content Calendar"},{"id":50,"owner":"Juli","description":"Follow up with Anna about her article","status":"open","context":"Still outstanding.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":51,"owner":"Juli","description":"Return Jocelyn's call","status":"open","context":"Still owed, connect this week.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Other"},{"id":52,"owner":"Juli","description":"Flag rogue Facebook group comments/page posts in WhatsApp","status":"open","context":"Screenshot and flag if no time to remove directly. Pages commenting = automatic removal, competitor group promos = remove comment + person. AdVent Technologies flagged as one to remove.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Social"},{"id":53,"owner":"Juli","description":"Continue filming short videos, send raw footage to Lucas","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":37,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Meet with GetVWire to determine Mariannel vs. Michelle going forward","status":"open","context":"Monday Sep 15. Until then, don't assign Michelle anything major.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Team"},{"id":38,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Cherry call - content strategy + possible events partnership","status":"open","context":"Monday Sep 15 @ 10am. Contact: Jason (marketing, based in Israel).","completed_at":null,"topic":"Sponsors"},{"id":39,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Follow up with Vine Dental's Andy about scheduling a meeting","status":"open","context":"Andy hasn't confirmed a meeting yet.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Sponsors"},{"id":40,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Send Juli the Advisory Board mastermind recap","status":"open","context":"Still owed from last week.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Advisory Board"},{"id":41,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Review the 3 video versions Lucas sent and pick a direction","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":42,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Put together a marketing package concept for Revenue Well","status":"open","context":"They're happy and asking about a formal package.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Sponsors"},{"id":43,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Look into Vine Dental's October event as a potential tag-on opportunity","status":"open","context":"Vine Dental's Accelerate Revenue Workshop, Oct 22-24. New events model: tag onto sponsor events instead of running DOMA's own.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Events"},{"id":54,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Add Cherry and Vine Dental logos to homepage sponsor carousel and Offers page","status":"open","context":"Describe what they do, link to their main websites for now. Juli sending links via WhatsApp.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Website"},{"id":55,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Create welcome image for new sponsors - FB Page + group announcement","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Sponsors"},{"id":56,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Remove Mark3 from everywhere on the website","status":"open","context":"Relationship ended after 6 months - they wanted guarantees DOMA couldn't provide.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Website"},{"id":57,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Fix the Roya logo - currently unreadable","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Website"},{"id":58,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Add an email performance tab to the dashboard","status":"done","context":null,"completed_at":"2026-09-11 19:35:56","topic":"Dashboard"},{"id":59,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Finalize Juli's video","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":60,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Keep sending newsletters through ActiveCampaign, keep monitoring AC vs. GoHighLevel","status":"open","context":"Sep 2 send: AC 1,019 unique opens vs. GHL 83 opens same day. GHL emails appear to be landing in spam for many recipients.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Email"},{"id":61,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Get familiar with Replit when bandwidth allows","status":"open","context":"For the Ask DOMA tool Kyle is building there.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Other"},{"id":62,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Check which content calendar items are not going live and why, sync with Juli","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Content Calendar"}]},{"id":3,"meeting_date":"2026-09-04","title":"Juli & Lucas Check-in Recap","summary":"Juli sent Lucas her first video for editing; polls going into FB content through September to boost survey response; Anna's front desk turnover article lined up for blog + newsletter; Ask DOMA concept validated as feasible with Lucas. Open questions for Kyle: Advisory Board call recap for the group follow-up + Sept 25 agenda, clearer cohort/mastermind vision before the 25th, and whether to keep hand-picking Mariannel's topics or let the dashboard suggest them.","raw_notes":"Quick recap from the call with Lucas and I this morning and a few things I wanted to keep on your radar.\n👇\n\n🎥 Video\nI completed and sent Lucas my first video, and he's working on the edit now. He'll send it back to me to review before it goes out. Assuming this first one works well, I'd like to continue building these into the content mix.\n\n👥 Advisory Board\nWe talked about the limited survey response and making it easier for people to give us feedback. Lucas is going to work some simple polls into the FB content through September.\n\nWhen you have a chance, I'd still love your thoughts/recap from the last Advisory Board call so I can send a follow-up to the group like I did after the previous meeting. It would also help us start building the agenda for the September 25 meeting.\n\nI'd also like to get a little clearer on your vision for the cohort/mastermind piece before the 25th, so we can use the next meeting to move that conversation forward in the direction you're envisioning.\n\n📅 Content Calendar / Automation\nLucas said the calendar has been helpful and that his workload feels manageable. We talked about using analytics + AI to generate content/topic suggestions and potentially automate more of the process.\n\nOne question for you on Mariannel's content - do you want to continue sending her the sponsor/eBook topics, or would you be comfortable with us beginning to pull appropriate topic suggestions from the Dashboard?\n\nI'm going to touch base with Mariannel this morning about her current posting schedule/process so we can figure out the cleanest way to incorporate her content into the calendar and ideally automate as much of it as makes sense.\n\n✍️ Content\nAnna's front desk turnover article is planned for the blog next week and the newsletter. Lucas is also going back through existing podcasts for insurance-verification content we could repurpose into video/social and potentially connect to a sponsor.\n\n💡 Ask DOMA\nI walked Lucas through more of the concept we discussed. He feels the basic idea is feasible - trusted/searchable resources, video, customization, compliance possibilities and potentially a subscription component. We touched briefly on pricing, but I think this is something we can continue developing rather than trying to solve all at once.\n\n📸 Archy\nWe also talked about trying to get some video/stills from the October meeting that we could repurpose for future content.\n\n🎙️ Podcast\nAnd just keeping our September 21 podcast on the radar. I'll make sure I'm prepared on my end.\n\nI think that captures the main pieces from this morning. Mostly wanted to keep you in the loop, get a little direction on the pieces above, and make sure what Lucas and I are working on continues to line up with where you see things going. 😊\n","action_items":[{"id":28,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Send Juli a recap/thoughts from the last Advisory Board call","status":"open","context":"So Juli can send a follow-up to the group like she did after the previous meeting, and start building the agenda for the September 25 meeting.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Advisory Board"},{"id":29,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Get clearer with Juli on the cohort/mastermind vision before September 25","status":"open","context":"So the next Advisory Board meeting can move that conversation forward in the direction Kyle is envisioning.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Mastermind"},{"id":31,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Decide: keep sending Mariannel sponsor/ebook topics directly, or let the dashboard pull topic suggestions for her","status":"open","context":"Juli is touching base with Mariannel about her current posting schedule/process to figure out the cleanest way to fold her content into the calendar and automate what makes sense.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":34,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Keep developing the Ask DOMA concept","status":"open","context":"Trusted/searchable resources, video, customization, compliance, and a possible subscription component. Pricing touched on briefly - not trying to solve all at once.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Ask DOMA"},{"id":36,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Be prepared for the September 21 podcast","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Podcast"},{"id":27,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Edit Juli's first video and send it back to her for review","status":"open","context":"Juli sent Lucas her first video. If it works well, more of these get built into the content mix.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":30,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Work simple polls into the Facebook content through September","status":"open","context":"Response rate on the survey has been limited - polls are an easier way for people to give feedback.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Advisory Board"},{"id":32,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Publish Anna's front desk turnover article - blog next week and the newsletter","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":33,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Go back through existing podcasts for insurance-verification content to repurpose into video/social","status":"open","context":"Potentially tie it to a sponsor.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":35,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Get video/stills from the October meeting to repurpose for future content","status":"open","context":"Via Archy.","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"}]},{"id":2,"meeting_date":"2026-08-31","title":"DOMA Team Meeting Recap","summary":"Dashboard walkthrough with Juli; locked in search/discovery upgrades for ebooks and sponsor resources; separated to-do tab from content calendar; newsletter and next-meeting timing confirmed.","raw_notes":"WhatsApp recap (paste-ready)\n\nHey team, quick recap from this morning so we're all on the same page 👇\n\nWe're in good shape — dashboard's working well, leads are climbing, SEO position is trending up.\n\nLucas\n\nSplit the To-Do tab off from the Content Calendar so they don't cross over\nAdd a search bar to the ebooks so we can pull the right one fast when someone asks a question in the group\nSame idea for sponsors — searchable by pain point/topic (like \"phone service\") so we can recommend the right company quick\nAdd the blog articles into the Useful Links section too\nSend me the newsletter today for a final look before it goes out Wednesday\nWhen you get a minute, take a look at whether this dashboard setup could realistically be packaged and sold to practices down the line — no rush, just want your read on it\nKeep moving on the existing stuff: duplicate meta description fix, Facebook API reach data pull, blog articles for the two top ebooks, CTA on ebook thank-you pages\n\nJuli\n\nAdd Mariannel's sponsor post content into the shared calendar so we're not duplicating and sponsors get even coverage\nGet that first short video done and over to Lucas by end of week\nKeep the survey follow-ups going — only one back so far\n\nMe\n\nSending you (Juli) the mastermind/cohort breakdown doc today\nFilming videos and getting emails out today\n\nNewsletter goes out Wednesday the 2nd. Next meeting — thinking Friday the 4th before Labor Day, 7am if we can swing it. I'll confirm Thursday once I know my travel schedule. Talk soon.\n\nNew dashboard tickets (for Lucas to add)\n\nDOMA Team Meeting Recap — Aug 31, 2026\nDashboard walkthrough with Juli; locked in search/discovery upgrades for ebooks and sponsor resources; separated to-do tab from content calendar; newsletter and next-meeting timing confirmed.\n\nTo Do\n\nPerson | Subject | Title | Notes\nLucas | Dashboard | Create separate To-Do tab, split from Content Calendar | Keeps meeting to-dos from crossing with content scheduling\nLucas | Dashboard | Add search bar to ebooks section | Search by topic to quickly surface the right ebook link for member questions\nLucas | Dashboard | Add searchable sponsor/resource directory | Pull sponsor companies by pain point (e.g. \"phone service\") for fast recommendations\nLucas | Content | Add blog articles into Useful Links section |\nLucas | Content | Send newsletter to Kyle for final review | Needs to go out Wed Sept 2\nLucas | Other | Assess feasibility of packaging dashboard as a sellable product | Exploratory only, no timeline yet\nJuli | Content | Add Mariannel's sponsor post content into shared content calendar | Prevents duplicate sponsor coverage, keeps exposure even\nJuli | Other | Continue survey follow-ups | 1 response in so far, reminder already sent\nKyle | Mastermind | Send Juli the advisory board / cohort breakdown doc |\n\nIn Progress (carrying over)\n\nJuli / Content — Finish first short video, send raw footage to Lucas by end of week\n\nTeam\n\nNext meeting: Friday, Sept 4 — targeting 7am ET, Kyle confirming Thursday based on travel\n","action_items":[{"id":23,"owner":"Juli","description":"Add Mariannel's sponsor post content into shared content calendar","status":"open","context":"Prevents duplicate sponsor coverage, keeps exposure even","completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":24,"owner":"Juli","description":"Continue survey follow-ups","status":"open","context":"1 response in so far, reminder already sent","completed_at":null,"topic":"Other"},{"id":26,"owner":"Juli","description":"Finish first short video, send raw footage to Lucas by end of week","status":"done","context":"Carrying over from the Aug 31 meeting","completed_at":"2026-09-09 22:06:28","topic":"Content"},{"id":25,"owner":"Kyle","description":"Send Juli the advisory board / cohort breakdown doc","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Mastermind"},{"id":17,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Create separate To-Do tab, split from Content Calendar","status":"open","context":"Keeps meeting to-dos from crossing with content scheduling","completed_at":null,"topic":"Dashboard"},{"id":18,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Add search bar to ebooks section","status":"open","context":"Search by topic to quickly surface the right ebook link for member questions","completed_at":null,"topic":"Dashboard"},{"id":19,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Add searchable sponsor/resource directory","status":"open","context":"Pull sponsor companies by pain point (e.g. \"phone service\") for fast recommendations","completed_at":null,"topic":"Dashboard"},{"id":20,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Add blog articles into Useful Links section","status":"open","context":null,"completed_at":null,"topic":"Content"},{"id":21,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Send newsletter to Kyle for final review","status":"done","context":"Needs to go out Wed Sept 2","completed_at":"2026-09-09 22:08:05","topic":"Content"},{"id":22,"owner":"Lucas","description":"Assess feasibility of packaging dashboard as a sellable product","status":"open","context":"Exploratory only, no timeline yet","completed_at":null,"topic":"Other"}]},{"id":1,"meeting_date":"2026-08-24","title":"DOMA Team Meeting Recap","summary":"Podcast (Sept 21) direction locked in; deep mastermind strategy discussion (exclusivity/application model, pod leaders, ~$199/mo + affiliate structure); reviewed the analytics dashboard (newsletter, GSC, GHL leads, ebook performance, Instagram); Juli starting video content this week.","raw_notes":"👋 DOMA Team Meeting Recap (Aug 24)\nKyle, Lucas & Juli\n\nLots covered today — metrics, mastermind strategy, content direction, and video plans! Here's everything 👇\n\n🎙️ PODCAST — SEPTEMBER 21ST\nJuli sent over a podcast outline — great work! Kyle reviewed it and loves the structure. A few direction notes:\n\nThe podcast should subtly introduce the mastermind concept — not a hard pitch, but planting the seed so listeners think \"what is that?\"\nFocus on Kyle's story, DOMA's history, and the community/support angle — that's the heart of what the mastermind is about\nDate locked: Monday September 21st @ 11am ET\nJuli to ask Mariannel to set up the Zoom and add both Kyle and Juli\n\n🧠 MASTERMIND — STRATEGY EVOLUTION\n\nBig thinking happened on this today. Here's where the concept is landing:\n\nThe Rolex Model — Exclusivity Matters\nThe mastermind should NOT be open to everyone. People want what they can't easily have. Like Rolex — you apply, you wait, you get accepted. This creates desire and perceived value. The journey to get IN is part of the value.\n\nAdmission Requirements (to be finalized):\nPeople will need to earn their way in. Possible criteria being considered:\n\nMinimum years in dentistry\nPublished article on the DOMA website\nApplication + vetting process\nDemonstrated commitment to giving before taking\n\nWhat Makes DOMA's Mastermind Different:\nMost \"masterminds\" are just Zoom sessions where someone talks at you. A real mastermind is collaborative problem-solving — every member brings their specific challenge to the group and others who've been there help guide them through it. That's what we're building.\n\nPod Leader Model:\n\nPod leaders run small groups (10–15 people) with a specific niche/specialty\nExample: Juli could lead a pod for office managers who want to get out of the practice or transition into consulting\nAnother pod leader might focus on scaling an existing business\nPod leaders need to be paid — the revenue model needs to account for this\n\nMembership + Affiliate Model (being explored):\n\nBallpark: ~$199/month per member\nIf a member refers 2 people → their membership is free\nThis creates organic growth without it feeling like a pyramid structure\nPod leaders get a cut of the members in their pod\n\nKey Questions for the Advisory Board on Friday:\n\nWho would be paying for the mastermind — you personally or your practice?\nWhat does \"elevated\" look like for you — staying in dentistry but growing, or getting out entirely?\nWhen you hear \"mastermind\" — what do you envision?\nWhat would make you commit month after month?\n\nKyle will pull today's transcript into Granola and build out a focused questionnaire to add to Juli's session 2 agenda.\n\nCoaches & Consultants Vetting:\nWe're still planning to post in the group looking for coaches and consultants to connect with. The test is simple — ask them to write an article. Who follows through tells you everything. Kyle doesn't work with takers. The people who give first are the ones we want in the room.\n\n📊 METRICS DASHBOARD — WHAT LUCAS BUILT\n\nLucas built out a full analytics dashboard — great work! Here's what we reviewed:\n\nNewsletter (Aug 6th send):\n\nOpen rate: 20% ✅\nTop clicked: Join the Community\n2nd: Black Diamond Radio\n3rd: Blog article\n\nGoogle Search Console (last 7 days):\n\nTotal clicks: 41\nTop queries: \"dental office manager,\" \"dental office management training,\" \"dental office manager training manual PDF\"\nAverage position: improving — still work to do on click-through rate (target 2–3%)\nMost traffic on mobile — desktop is secondary\nAction: Lucas to add search volume data to the dashboard so we know which keywords are worth targeting\nAction: Fix duplicate meta description on one page (not critical but needs cleaning)\n\nContent Gap Opportunities spotted:\n\n\"Dental office management tips\"\n\"Managing a dental office\"\n\"Dental coaching\"\n\n→ These should inform upcoming blog articles\n\nTop Performing Ebooks (last 30 days):\n\n\"10 Reports Every Dental Office Manager Should Look At\" — 51 views 🔥\n\"Your First 90 Days as a Dental Office Manager\" — 23–41 views 🔥\n\"What to Say When the Doctor Won't Listen\" — posted Friday Aug 22nd, only 4 downloads so far — likely timing issue (Friday = bad day to post)\n\"Schedule Like a Boss\" — low views, needs a repost\n\nKey insight from metrics:\nThe ebooks are telling us exactly what people want. Stop guessing. Use ebook performance data to drive ALL content decisions going forward.\n\nThe New Content Rhythm:\n\nPost ebook → track performance\nIf it performs well → record a video on that topic\nTurn it into a blog article\nFeature it in the newsletter\nOne high-performing ebook → multiple pieces of content\n\nInstagram:\n\nBest day to post: Tuesday\nBest time: 9am ET\nPhotos are largely dead on Instagram — people want video and carousel/swipe content\n26 reach on Friday but only 1 click — performance is low on static images\n\nGoHighLevel Leads (last 7 days):\n\n22 new leads\nTop sources: Free Starter Kit + ebook downloads\n51 leads in the last 5 days during a spike — likely tied to the Revenue Well email send on the 19th. Lucas to verify what caused the spike\n\n🎥 VIDEO CONTENT — JULI STARTING THIS WEEK\n\nKyle encouraged Juli to start filming videos — she's in. A few things Kyle shared:\n\nDon't wait for perfect — put your reps in and get better over time\nFrame all content as \"this is what has worked for me\" — no one can argue with your personal experience\nThis eliminates the fear of being called out and gives you freedom to speak authentically\nLucas will edit and cut the raw footage into usable clips\n\nVideos Kyle is going to record based on ebook data:\n\n\"10 Reports Every Dental Office Manager Should Look at Each Month\"\n\"Your First 90 Days as a Dental Office Manager\"\n\nThese will also become blog articles.\n\n✅ KYLE — ACTION ITEMS\n\nRecord videos on the two top-performing ebook topics (10 Reports + First 90 Days)\n\n✅ JULI — ACTION ITEMS\n\nAsk Mariannel to set up the podcast Zoom for Monday September 21st @ 11am ET — add both Kyle and Juli\nAsk Mariannel to repost the \"What to Say When the Doctor Won't Listen\" ebook — Friday timing was bad, needs a proper mid-week repost\nAsk Mariannel to repost \"Schedule Like a Boss\" — low views, needs another push\nFollow up with Anna today about the article — she said she would write one and hasn't followed through yet\nStart filming short videos this week — send raw footage to Lucas to edit\nReview the advisory board session 2 agenda and add mastermind-focused questions based on today's conversation\nKeep populating content calendar 2 weeks ahead — use ebook performance data to guide topics\n\n✅ LUCAS — ACTION ITEMS\n\nAdd search volume data to the dashboard for all keyword queries\nFix duplicate meta description on the flagged page\nInvestigate what caused the spike on Aug 19th — was it the Revenue Well email?\nSet best post time on all platforms to Tuesday @ 9am ET\nCheck why Facebook API isn't pulling reach data into the dashboard\nCreate blog articles for the two top-performing ebooks (10 Reports + First 90 Days) — start here before the other content calendar items\nAdd CTA to each ebook's thank you page → download button + blog article link\nContinue building dashboard with GoHighLevel lead data, social data, and ebook performance week over week\n\n🗓️ UPCOMING\n\nFriday Aug 28 @ 11am ET — Advisory Board Session 2 (mastermind questions on the agenda)\nMonday Aug 31 @ 9am ET — Team meeting (normal time)\nMonday Sept 7 — No meeting (Labor Day)\nMonday Sept 2 @ 9am ET — Newsletter sends via ActiveCampaign 🚀\nSunday Sept 21 @ 11am ET — Kyle & Juli podcast recording\n","action_items":[{"id":2,"owner":"Juli","description":"Ask Mariannel to set up the podcast Zoom for Monday September 21st @ 11am ET","status":"o